{{ define "title_rules" -}}
The title names what the entry is about, for a reader scanning a list of entries: 3 to 5 plain words, at most 32 characters, a noun phrase rather than a sentence — like `daemon project removal`. Name the subject, never the entry's role in the graph: no framing words such as decision, directive, plan, signal, gap, entry or commits, no entry IDs, no trailing punctuation. Write it in the graph's configured authoring language: {{ if .ConfiguredLanguage }}`{{ .ConfiguredLanguage }}`{{ else }}English (no language configured){{ end }}, with that language's normal capitalization.

Related entries below carry their titles. Reuse a related entry's title only when this entry is about exactly the same subject; when its subject differs, the title names what differs, in subject words.
{{- end }}

